🔹 🎯 Task 2: Wrapper Comparison and Caching
You are testing how Integer objects compare using == and equals().
📥 Input:
Integer a = 100;
Integer b = 100;
Integer c = 200;
Integer d = 200;
⚙️ Requirements:
• Compare a and b using reference comparison and value comparison
• Compare c and d using reference comparison and value comparison
• Print results in this order:
"a == b: <true/false>"
"a.equals(b): <true/false>"
"c == d: <true/false>"
"c.equals(d): <true/false>"
📌 Constraints:
• Use only standard Java
• Output must match the required format exactly
📤 Output format:
a == b: <true/false>
a.equals(b): <true/false>
c == d: <true/false>
c.equals(d): <true/false>
📌 Test cases:
Input: a=100, b=100, c=200, d=200
Output:
a == b: true
a.equals(b): true
c == d: false
c.equals(d): true

